**Topic diversity** is the share of unique words among the top 10 words of all topics. 1.0 would mean no topic shares a top word with another. At 0.729, most topics are described by their own words.

**Cohesion** is the average cosine similarity between each paper in a topic and the center of that topic. The same measure over the whole corpus is 0.517, so papers within a topic are clearly more similar to each other than papers taken at random. Every topic scored above that baseline. The weakest topics were 0 (0.609), 4 and 9 (0.616), 8 (0.618) and 35 (0.626).

