After reassignment, BERTopic recalculates topic representations from c-TF-IDF instead of embedding centers. Merging topics after this step is not supported, so `--nr-topics` is applied before reassignment.

### 3.2 Short documents

Papers with fewer than 60 words are marked `short_doc`, since topics based on very little text are less reliable. **No paper in this corpus is that short**, because the corpus build step already removes documents under 20 words and arXiv abstracts are much longer. The check stays in the code so it covers future data sources.

### 3.3 Jargon

Two kinds of jargon were handled:

- **Words in every abstract.** Without the domain stop word list, labels filled up with words such as "propose" and "model". These are removed before topic words are chosen.
- **Words shared by many topics.** After fitting, any word that appears in the top 10 of 25% or more of the topics is reported as a stop word candidate. No word reached that level in the final run.

Technical terms that do identify a topic, such as "diffusion", "pde" or "eeg", are kept on purpose.

## 4. Entity results

### 4.1 Plain spaCy

The first run used spaCy without changes.

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Time for 5,007 papers | 121.8 s (41 papers per second) |
| Papers with at least one entity | 4,860 (97.1%) |
| ORG / PRODUCT / PERSON / GPE / LANGUAGE | 17,021 / 879 / 5,201 / 1,526 / 76 |

The most frequent entities show how the model, trained mostly on news text, handles AI papers:

| Model output | Actual meaning |
|---|---|
| LLM, AI, GPU, RL, linear as **ORG** | general terms |
| Gaussian, Markov, Monte Carlo as **PERSON** | mathematical terms named after people |
| Qwen as **PERSON**, Qwen3 as **GPE** | a model family |
| F1, node, AI as **GPE** | a metric and general words |

Languages (English, Arabic, Spanish, Chinese) and some model names (DeepSeek, Llama) were labeled correctly.

### 4.2 Jargon filter and rules

Three changes were added on top of spaCy:

1. **Entity rules** run before spaCy's own model and tag known names: model families matching a pattern such as GPT, Llama, Qwen, DeepSeek, Mistral, Gemma, Claude, Gemini or BERT, plus versions like Qwen3 and GPT-4o, as `PRODUCT`. Common datasets and benchmarks (ImageNet, MMLU, GSM8K, HumanEval and others) are also tagged `PRODUCT`, and major labs and companies `ORG`.
2. **A jargon list** of general and mathematical terms (LLM, RL, GPU, Gaussian, Markov, Fourier, F1 and others) is never kept as an entity.
3. **Lowercase spans are dropped**, since real names are capitalized.

| Metric | Plain spaCy | With rules |
|---|---|---|
| Time for 5,007 papers | 121.8 s | 126.4 s |
| Papers with at least one entity | 97.1% | 95.0% |
| ORG | 17,021 | 14,635 |
| PRODUCT | 879 | 1,997 |
| PERSON | 5,201 | 4,264 |
| GPE | 1,526 | 979 |
| LANGUAGE | 76 | 76 |

`PRODUCT` more than doubled, and its most frequent entries are now Qwen3, Claude, Qwen2.5, Qwen and DeepSeek. The fixed false positives are gone from the top of every list. The rules add about 4% to the running time.

Errors that remained in the most frequent entities:

- method acronyms as ORG: GRPO, QA, ML, OPD
- optimizers and mathematical terms as PERSON or GPE: Adam, Muon, Wasserstein, Newton, ReLU
- fragments of LaTeX: K$

A further filter covers these: more terms in the jargon list, removal of spans containing `$`, and removal of short all-capital ORG spans that are not known organizations.

