## 5. Filtered retrieval

### 5.1 Stored metadata

Topic and entity metadata is added to every ChromaDB record during ingest:

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `topic` | int | Topic number, -1 for outliers |
| `topic_label` | str | Name from the manual review if one was given, otherwise the top three words |
| `topic_reassigned` | bool | True if the topic came from outlier reassignment |
| `topic_prob` | float | HDBSCAN confidence, only for papers placed directly in a topic |
| `entities` | str | Readable list, such as `OpenAI (ORG), GPT-4 (PRODUCT)` |
| `n_entities` | int | Number of entities |
| `ent_<name>` | bool | One flag per entity, such as `ent_qwen3 = true` |

Each entity is stored as its own true/false flag because ChromaDB filters work reliably on simple values in every version, while list values are not supported everywhere. Entity names are lowercased and non-alphanumeric characters become underscores, so "GPT-4" becomes `ent_gpt_4`.

The metadata is added during ingest instead of being patched onto existing records. Running `ingest --reset` therefore always rebuilds a clean collection, with no entity flags left over from earlier runs.

### 5.2 Usage

```bash
python src/vector_store.py topics
python src/vector_store.py search "reward models for alignment" --topic 0
python src/vector_store.py search "open-weight model evaluation" --entity Qwen3
python src/vector_store.py search "tool use" --topic 0 --no-reassigned
```

Filters are passed to ChromaDB as a `where` condition, so the similarity search only considers matching records. Several filters are combined with `$and`.

### 5.3 Edge cases

| Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| Topic number does not exist | Message pointing to the `topics` command |
| Entity not mentioned by any paper | "No results match this filter" |
| Collection ingested before topics and entities existed | Message asking to run `ingest --reset` |
| NLP files missing during ingest | Ingest continues without that metadata and prints a note |
| Several filters at once | Combined with `$and` |
| Topic names changed after the manual review | Picked up on the next `ingest --reset` |

